Z||000007||Oreif||12-28-2001||10:30 PM||||I am working on my Fiero model. I have to still locate an IMSA spoiler or make my own. The hood vents are almost done. I still need some other items for the interior and engine compartment. (wires, hoses, mounts, trunk carpet, etc) I usually work on Ships. Here are some pics of an Aircraft Carrier I did it is over 39" long. All the rails, stairs, antenna's, airplane landing gear, and safty nets are etched brass. I am working on a Battleship (USS New Jersy) You can see the brass that I have added and what the brass sheets look like. <P>This is usually what I do on Sunday Nights from 9pm until 1am.<P>(Or on the nights I am off of work like tonight.)<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Ships1.JPG">  <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ships2.JPG">  <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/NJ1.JPG">  <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Etch1.JPG">  <P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">            <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 12-28-2001).]||||reg||1
