Z||000013||Sage||12-29-2001||10:30 AM||||Fantastic work, everybody!  Don't want to single anybody out, as all of the examples are exquisite.  Could go on and on about any one of them.  Easy to see the many hours of love that went into all of the examples displayed.  Roger, you have to get the major kudos on volume alone, but it is not hard to see the time and attention to detail that went into all of these projects.  <P>Have done some of this myself in my younger years and still have a couple left, but don't have a digital camera capable of doing any of it justice, so will not attempt to post pics at this time.<P>Oreif, I once made a spoiler for a 67 Camaro out of an old toothbrush handle, worked pretty well too!<P>Not hard to see why you guys have some of the best looking full size Fieros around, as from these pics, all of you have the dedication to do whatever it takes to produce the results you have imagined.<P>Great job everybody, I'm thoroughly impressed.  Thanks for sharing.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Have a good one!||||reg||1
